<edge source="iran_hormuz_standoff::maritime_incident_rate" target="allied_arms_reshaping::deployment_tempo" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">A rising rate of hostile or hazardous incidents in the strait triggers immediate naval and air escort taskings, emergency patrols and forward rotations to protect transits, raising the rate of unit dispatches and rotations.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_hormuz_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">allied_arms_reshaping</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_hormuz_standoff::maritime_incident_rate" target="israel_lebanon_conflict::crossborder_incidents" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A spike in hostile incidents against vessels in the Strait leads Tehran to order or encourage Hezbollah cross-border strikes and probing attacks to impose costs and divert adversary resources, causing more Lebanon–Israel border incidents within weeks.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_hormuz_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">israel_lebanon_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_hormuz_standoff::maritime_incident_rate" target="russia_ukraine_blacksea::drone_strike_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">A spike in hostile incidents in the Strait draws US/UK/French naval and air assets and ISR towards the Gulf, reducing Western presence and air/sea-based sensor/defense coverage in the Black Sea and thereby lowering deterrence and enabling a higher tempo of drone/missile strikes there.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_hormuz_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_blacksea</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_hormuz_standoff::maritime_incident_rate" target="us_china_rivalry::export_control_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained rise in hostile incidents in the Strait provides political cover and evidentiary pretexts for the US to broaden export controls and sanctions on firms (including Chinese intermediaries) accused of enabling Iranian maritime or military activity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_hormuz_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
