<edge source="us_china_rivalry::supply_diversification" target="allied_arms_reshaping::deployment_tempo" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Allied diversification of suppliers, routes and inventories reduces single‑point chokepoints and logistical friction, enabling more frequent rotations and sustained higher tempo of deployments.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">allied_arms_reshaping</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_rivalry::supply_diversification" target="iran_hormuz_standoff::rerouted_trade_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">As importers and shippers respond to US–China rivalry by diversifying sourcing and routes away from chokepoints tied to contested actors, a greater share of cargo and energy shipments is actively diverted from the Strait onto alternate sea lanes and pipelines.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_hormuz_standoff</data>
</edge>
