</edge>
<edge source="allied_arms_reshaping::deployment_tempo" target="iran_hormuz_standoff::maritime_incident_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">A higher tempo of allied unit and platform transits and rotations through the Strait increases the number of close encounters, interdiction attempts, and platform interactions, raising the raw frequency of collisions, confrontations and other maritime incidents.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">allied_arms_reshaping</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_hormuz_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="allied_arms_reshaping::deployment_tempo" target="israel_lebanon_conflict::crossborder_incidents" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">An uptick in allied deployments (carrier/air assets, patrols, ISR platforms) in the Eastern Mediterranean and northern Israel/Lebanon border raises deterrence and disrupts militant movement and launch preparations, reducing the frequency of cross-border incursions and strikes.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">allied_arms_reshaping</data>
  <data key="d40">israel_lebanon_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="allied_arms_reshaping::deployment_tempo" target="russia_ukraine_blacksea::maritime_throughput" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased allied naval and mine-countermeasure deployments to the Black Sea region provide escorts, clearance and visible deterrence that reduce commercial risk perceptions and allow more commercial transits and cargo movements.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">allied_arms_reshaping</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_blacksea</data>
</edge>
