  <data key="d28">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="allied_arms_reshaping::operational_readiness" target="allied_arms_reshaping::deterrence_effectiveness" id="0">
  <data key="d28">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="allied_arms_reshaping::operational_readiness" target="allied_arms_reshaping::force_protection_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d28">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
</edge>
<edge source="allied_arms_reshaping::operational_readiness" target="iran_hormuz_standoff::strait_control_perc" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Improved allied operational readiness (sustained presence, quicker response, trained crews) leads market actors and regional players to perceive that allied forces can and will enforce safe passage, thereby increasing the perceived degree of allied control over the Strait.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">allied_arms_reshaping</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_hormuz_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="allied_arms_reshaping::operational_readiness" target="russia_ukraine_blacksea::grain_export_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher readiness of escort, minesweeping and port-handling units (driven by allied training, repairs and spares) increases safe sortie rates for grain shipments and steady port operations, raising export throughput.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">allied_arms_reshaping</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_blacksea</data>
</edge>
<edge source="allied_arms_reshaping::operational_readiness" target="us_china_rivalry::supply_diversification" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher readiness requirements force defense logisticians to contract multiple suppliers and establish alternative logistics routes to avoid single‑source failures, increasing the geographic and supplier diversity of critical supply chains.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">allied_arms_reshaping</data>
