<edge source="allied_arms_reshaping::regional_security_tensio" target="iran_hormuz_standoff::rerouted_trade_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising regional friction and perceived escalation risk prompts shippers and insurers to choose longer but safer alternative routes or modalities, increasing the volume of cargo and energy shipments deliberately rerouted away from the Strait even absent a specific incident.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">allied_arms_reshaping</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_hormuz_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="allied_arms_reshaping::regional_security_tensio" target="israel_lebanon_conflict::diplomatic_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising allied-driven regional tensions (escalatory postures, incidents, or shows of force) prompt external states and international organizations to step up diplomatic interventions, sanctions-threats, and shuttle diplomacy to prevent wider escalation.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">allied_arms_reshaping</data>
  <data key="d40">israel_lebanon_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="allied_arms_reshaping::regional_security_tensio" target="us_china_rivalry::tech_investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Escalating regional tensions prompt immediate public budget ramps and private capital reallocation toward defense-relevant tech (AI, secure communications, chips) driven by expected demand and government co-financing programs.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">allied_arms_reshaping</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
